CFG722: bridge astra's unsolved cold-energy kinetic equation (Supplement E selector) to the P-field action (CFG694/695).
Criteria: FROZEN_CRITERIA.md (committed alone, cb2aac21f). kappa = 1/2 FITTED; footings never pooled; the cold energy's mass is
required; not "theory closed". Analytic + small numerics only (no PM, no merger simulation, no download).
Run:  nice -n 10 python3 cfg722.py        (CFG722_MUTATE=1: lambda -> 0, saturation 2 a0, tether sign; exit 1 iff all bite)

=== B1 (Q1) bound-charge neutrality: Hernquist 1e11 Msun, a = 3 kpc, P tapered to 0 over [r_e, 1.1 r_e], r_e = 300 kpc
  canonical: M_c(<r_e) Gauss 2.3856e+12 Msun (= 23.856 M_b); numerical inside 2.3852e+12; edge shell -2.3852e+12; NET -6.407e+00 Msun, |net|/M_c = 2.69e-12 -> PASS
  alt: M_c(<r_e) Gauss 2.6273e+12 Msun (= 26.273 M_b); numerical inside 2.6269e+12; edge shell -2.6269e+12; NET -7.671e+00 Msun, |net|/M_c = 2.92e-12 -> PASS
  Reading: the bound charge only MOVES mass from the polarized region's edge to its interior; seen from outside the basin the
  system weighs M_b. It cannot supply CFG624's missing cold mass (X-COP 3.1/2.8 M_b, LG timing, mean density).

=== B2 (Q1) inertia and transport of the P field (linearised longitudinal sector, sympy)
  dispersion: omega = sqrt(K + gamma*k**2)/sqrt(I)   group velocity = gamma*k/(sqrt(I)*sqrt(K + gamma*k**2))
  Noether momentum density T^0x = -I*Derivative(P(x, t), t)*Derivative(P(x, t), x)  (set by I and grad P, not by the bound charge rho_c = div P)
  translating lump exp(-(x - v t)^2): residual / lump = -4*I*t**2*v**4 + 8*I*t*v**3*x - 4*I*v**2*x**2 + 2*I*v**2 - K + 4*gamma*t**2*v**2 - 8*gamma*t*v*x + 4*gamma*x**2 - 2*gamma
  -> zero for all x only if K = 0 and v^2 = gamma/I. A gapped (K > 0) field has no translating lump at any v: no ballistic,
     particle-like transport. The bound charge has no inertia of its own and no phase space; it cannot 'pass through' a merger.

