=== B5 (Q2) coupling ID: static energy U[u] = (1/4 pi G) int dV [w(u) - g_N u]; carrier mass fixed at M_law(<10 r_M)
  canonical M_b 1e10: M_c = 9.51 M_b; dU/(M_c V_f^2): s 0.5: +inf (wall at r<0.0001 r_M); s 0.8: -0.1363; s 1.25: +0.0954; s 2.0: +0.2249; s 4.0: +0.3254
  canonical M_b 1e12: M_c = 9.51 M_b; dU/(M_c V_f^2): s 0.5: +inf (wall at r<0.0001 r_M); s 0.8: -0.1363; s 1.25: +0.0954; s 2.0: +0.2249; s 4.0: +0.3254
  alt M_b 1e10: M_c = 9.51 M_b; dU/(M_c V_f^2): s 0.5: +inf (wall at r<0.0001 r_M); s 0.8: -0.1363; s 1.25: +0.0954; s 2.0: +0.2249; s 4.0: +0.3254
  alt M_b 1e12: M_c = 9.51 M_b; dU/(M_c V_f^2): s 0.5: +inf (wall at r<0.0001 r_M); s 0.8: -0.1363; s 1.25: +0.0954; s 2.0: +0.2249; s 4.0: +0.3254
  analytic: d^2/du^2 [tsign w(u) - g_N u] = -sigma*u*(-2*a_0 + u)/(-a_0 + u)**2  (> 0 on 0 < u < a0 for tsign = +1: pointwise convex; the truncated
  law is then the constrained minimiser at fixed carrier mass, since it is pointwise optimal wherever the mass cap does not bind)
  M3 note (POST-HOC, no verdict weight): with tsign = -1 the integrand is pointwise CONCAVE and B4 has no equilibrium root;
  the frozen M3 line (dU < 0 somewhere in the s-family) does not bite, because -g_N u dominates for stretched states and the
  compressed states (s < 1) sit beyond the wall in either sign.
  -> some dU < 0: the law is NOT the minimum
  IC-C analogue (law density, sigma = 0.05 V_f): the tether supplies the support astra's IC-C lacked, so the required exchange is its
  own kinetic energy, EXPORT 1.5 sigma^2 = 0.00375 M V_f^2 (astra, gravity only: IMPORT 0.50-0.64). IC-B-like (diffuse, s > 1): EXPORT.
  The bridge offers no export channel: P radiation is trapped (<= 1e-195, CFG659); phase mixing keeps the energy as dispersion.

